<topic id="GUID-0F3E5BD5-CA21-4B04-9BF5-33CED510DC8F" xml:lang="en-US"> 
  <title>Hot Spot Locations</title> 
  <body> 
	 <ul id="GUID-483BB591-3E5D-4D5E-AEA8-7AAAEF7A8B93"> 
		<li id="LI_4CB5918D2D464C67B091869DCF6CDCB1"> The die hot spot is shown to assist with heat pipe placement. It is recommended that the heat pipe be placed so that the active wick is directly over the hot spot. 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_3E760A2097C9459D9B5B79BA26609D5C">Since NVL series processors have multiple cores, there are multiple possible hot spot locations. As it is impossible to predict which core will be utilized in single threaded applications, a region is defined that envelopes all the cores. 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_A8F0322435B84B5EA8644845AD6F69AE">The region enveloping the cores is defined as the XY dimensions of a region and the XY coordinates to the center of that region, relative to Pin 1 package corner. 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_687884DFB339417F841F3596A83C5301">It is strongly recommended that the heat pipe be placed so that the active wick completely covers the hot spot region to safeguard against a moving hot spot. As well that thermal solution fully covers all tiles and not only compute hotspot. 
		</li> 
	 </ul> 
